An '''oil''' is a [[currency item]] that can be acquired from [[Blight (game mechanic)|Blight encounters]]. Using them on certain items gives these items an '''anointment''', which can modify them in various ways.

==Mechanics==
[[File:Annointing interface.png|thumb|right|400px|Sister Cassia's Anointing interface used to add the [[Command of Steel]] [[passive skill]] to an Amulet]]
Oils can be applied by the player via [[Cassia]], to [[blighted map]]s, [[ring]]s, [[amulet]]s or blight unique items in order to add an [[enchantment]] modifier to the item that have different effects based on the item type:

{| class="wikitable sortable"
! Type
! Oils
! Effect
|-
| [[Blighted map]]
| 1x-3x
| Increased monster pack size and effect depending on the oil
|-
| [[Blight-ravaged map]]
| 1x-9x
| Increased monster pack size and effect depending on the oil
|-
| [[Ring]]s
| 2x
| Buffs to [[Blight tower]]s
|-
| [[Amulet]]s<br>Blight unique items<br>{{il|Cord Belt}}
| 3x
| Allocate a [[notable passive skill]] from the [[passive skill tree]] without spending a skill point or being connected to the rest of the allocated skill tree.
|}

*'''Blighted maps''' can have up to three anointments at a time. [[blight-ravaged map]]s can have up to 9, with up to 3 of the same anointment. Multiple copies of the same oil are additive. ('''Example''' - 3 clear oil anointments with 10% reduced monster movement speed gives a total of 30%).

*'''Anointments''' on equipment take up an [[enchantment]] slot, shared with legacy [[Labyrinth enchantment]]s or enchantments from [[Harvest crafting]] or {{il|Tailoring Orb}}.

* You can acquire non-unique amulets with two random passives already anointed from Blight-ravaged maps which can be used as crafting bases.

*'''Corruption''' - [[Corrupt]]ing an item with an anointment causes it to retain its anointments, even if the outcome causes it to change its rarity. If the item had extra anointments, those will also be retained, even though it lost the modifier that allowed it to receive additional anointments. However, applying a new anointment without these modifiers will cause it to lose all its extra anointments.

* Allocated passive nodes on the Amulet behave as if the node were taken manually. In other words, socketing a Timeless Jewel and anointing a passive node will grant the new, transformed modifiers. It will not grant the old, original modifiers. You cannot allocate a [[Passive Mastery]] that is on the same passive cluster with the anointed notable, as it is not connected to your passive tree.

*'''Vendor''' - Three units of oil can be [[Vendor recipe system|vendored]] to create one vial of oil of the next tier, much like [[essence]]s. For example, one {{il|Golden Oil}} will require 3^12=531441 {{il|Clear Oil|Clear Oils}}. As such, it should only be used when one has a vast excess of one type of oil or needs a small amount of another type.

*'''Anointment order''' - There are 13 regular oils, combinations allow the use of the same oil more than once, and the order does not matter. All the notable passives which grant +30 to an attribute do not have an associated recipe.

*'''Prismatic Oil''' - {{il|Prismatic Oil}} is used to anoint exclusive notable passive skills not found on the passive skill tree.

*'''Tainted and Reflective Oil''' - {{il|Tainted Oil}} and {{il|Reflective Oil}} are not used for any anoint combinations, but are used in addition to allow anointment of [[corrupted]] or [[mirrored]] items, respectively.

*[[Talisman]]s cannot be anointed. Legacy talismans often dropped with a random anointment.

