==List of Anointable uniques==
These specific unique can also be [[List of anointments|anointed]], even if they are not an amulet or ring. They gain the same passive skills that those oils would apply to an amulet. These items can drop from completing Blighted maps or Blight-ravaged maps, with the exception of {{il|Stranglegasp}}, which only drops in Blight-ravaged maps, and {{il|Replica Stampede}}, which is only available as a reward from [[Grand Heist]]s.
* {{il|Breathstealer}}
* {{il|Cowl of the Cryophile}}
* {{il|Cowl of the Thermophile}}
* {{il|Cowl of the Ceraunophile}}
* {{il|Sporeguard}}
* {{il|The Stampede}} 
* {{il|Replica Stampede}}
* {{il|Stranglegasp}}
* {{il|Putrid Seed}}

Cowl of the Cryophile, Cowl of the Thermophile, and Cowl of the Ceraunophile can have up to two anointments, while Stranglegrasp can have up to four anointments.

Putrid Seed has its own mechanic that works differently from other anointable items. See its page for more details.

If a [[corruption]] results in turning these into a {{c|rare|Rare}} item, they will retain their anointments. With a {{il|Tainted Mythic Orb}}, it is possible to turn them into a different unique item of the same base item that normally cannot have anointments, or in the case of Stranglegasp, cannot have more than two anointments. Applying a new anointment to non-Blight uniques will cause them to lose any extra anointments beyond the default for their equipment type.

